  "description": "The All New Disc Brake Auro Triathlon & TT bike\n\nNewly reconfigured for 2021, the Auro Disc's most important update is the addition of hydraulic disc brakes. This update has led to a redesigned frame, now able to accommodate up to 28mm wide tyres, resulting in a much more aero profile with frame, rim and tyre widths all designed to work together to reduce drag. The fastest Vitus bike yet.\n\nKey features of the redesigned frame include a new headtube and stem design - still 100% integrated, but now much easier to travel with due to the lower stem cable guide, isolating the cables and allowing easy removal of the stem and handlebars. The frame tubes have been re-profiled taking maximum advantage of the UCI's rules on aerodynamic shapes. With the introduction of disc brakes wider tyers are now possible, which offers a distinct advantage to longer distance racing, particularly triathlon, where bigger volumes can rediuce rider fatigue and ease the run transition.\n\nThe Auro Disc CRS features Shimano's ever popular Ultegra 11 speed groupset, paired with Tektro HD-T190 hydraulic brakes. The build is completed with a full Vision cockpit, and Reynolds super fast AR 62/80 DB wheels.\n\nTT & Trialthlon disc brake frameset\n\nUp to 28mm tyre clearance\n\nFull internal cable routing\n\nShimano Ultegra 11 Speed\n\nReynolds AR62/80 DB Carbon wheelset\n\nVision cockpit",
